==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|anti|particle}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|anti-particle}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæntiˌpɑɹtɪkəl/}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|particle}} A [[subatomic particle]] corresponding to another [[particle]] with the same [[mass]], [[spin]] and [[mean]] [[lifetime]] but with [[charge]], [[parity]], [[strangeness]] and other [[quantum number]]s flipped in [[sign]]; a [[particle]] that has a reversed [[world line]] to another.
#* '''1988''', Stephen Hawking, ''A Brief History of Time: From the Big Bang to Black Holes'' (page 75)
#*: There could be whole antiworlds and antipeople made out of '''antiparticles'''. However, if you meet your antiself, don't shake hands!

